{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he awoke, etc. Surely, etc. and I, etc.</b> One needs to know the intent of his saying <b>surely</b> (אָכֵן), for it appears that what had been hidden was revealed to him. Further, what is this wonder <b>and I did not know</b> — for it appears that he needs to know everything that is hidden?" "And it may be explained along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Ḥullin 91b): ״כִּי בָא הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ״ — it set for him out of its season, so that he would sleep there in the inn of fortune, and Jacob did not sense the reason for the sun's setting out of its time. Therefore, when the dream came in great significance, then the hidden thing — the reason for the sun's setting — became known to him, and that is his saying ״אָכֵן יֵשׁ ה׳״ etc., and for this reason the sun set early for the purpose of sleeping in this place." "And his saying <b>there is HaShem</b> means that it is a place in which HaShem is present always more than in all other places, and that is why HaShem wished to speak with him there whenever he passed through there, and he said ״וְאָנֹכִי לֹא יָדָעְתִּי״ — before he grasped the reason for the thing, for had he known he would have prepared himself for prophecy, since prophecy requires preparation as is known. And it is possible that had he prepared himself, he would have prophesied while awake and [HaShem] would not have spoken to him in a dream; therefore he complains about the fact that he did not grasp the matter. And Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: 'Had I known, I would not have slept in a holy place' — end of quote. But if this alone was the intent, one may say to him: had you not slept, you would not have dreamed a prophetic dream with all those promises. So it is necessary to complete the intent with what I have explained."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:22.146903312Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}